      "text": "First, let's simplify the given equation. Let's set \\( y = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} \\). The equation then becomes:\n\\[\ny^2 + y = 12\n\\]\nThis can be rearranged into a standard quadratic equation:\n\\[\ny^2 + y - 12 = 0\n\\]\nNext, we solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\( y = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\), where \\( a = 1 \\), \\( b = 1 \\), and \\( c = -12 \\):\n\\[\ny = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot (-12)}}{2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1 + 48}}{2} = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} = \\frac{-1 \\pm 7}{2}\n\\]\nThis gives us two solutions:\n\\[\ny = \\frac{-1 + 7}{2} = 3 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad y = \\frac{-1 - 7}{2} = -4\n\\]\nSo, the possible values for \\( y \\) are \\( y = 3 \\) and \\( y = -4 \\).\n\nNow we substitute back \\( y = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} \\) to find the corresponding values of \\( x \\).\n\n1. For \\( y = 3 \\):\n\\[\n3 = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}\n\\]\nMultiplying both sides by \\( 3x-4 \\) gives:\n\\[\n3(3x-4) = 4x-16 \\implies 9x - 12 = 4x - 16 \\implies 5x = -4 \\implies x = -\\frac{4}{5}\n\\]\n\n2. For \\( y = -4 \\):\n\\[\n-4 = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}\n\\]\nMultiplying both sides by \\( 3x-4 \\) gives:\n\\[\n-4(3x-4) = 4x-16 \\implies -12x + 16 = 4x - 16 \\implies -16x = -32 \\implies x = 2\n\\]\n\nThe possible values of \\( x \\) are \\( x = -\\frac{4}{5} \\) and \\( x = 2 \\). The greatest possible value of \\( x \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
