      "text": "To solve the equation \\(\\left(\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}\\right) = 12\\), let's start by making a substitution to simplify the equation. Let \\( y = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} \\). Then the equation becomes:\n\n\\[ y^2 + y = 12. \\]\n\nRearrange this to form a standard quadratic equation:\n\n\\[ y^2 + y - 12 = 0. \\]\n\nNext, we solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\( y = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\), where \\( a = 1 \\), \\( b = 1 \\), and \\( c = -12 \\). Plugging in these values, we get:\n\n\\[ y = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot (-12)}}{2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1 + 48}}{2} = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} = \\frac{-1 \\pm 7}{2}. \\]\n\nThis gives us two solutions for \\( y \\):\n\n\\[ y = \\frac{-1 + 7}{2} = 3 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad y = \\frac{-1 - 7}{2} = -4. \\]\n\nSo, we have two cases to consider:\n\n1. \\( \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = 3 \\)\n2. \\( \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = -4 \\)\n\n**Case 1: \\( \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = 3 \\)**\n\nMultiply both sides by \\( 3x-4 \\):\n\n\\[ 4x - 16 = 3(3x - 4) \\]\n\\[ 4x - 16 = 9x - 12 \\]\n\\[ -16 + 12 = 9x - 4x \\]\n\\[ -4 = 5x \\]\n\\[ x = -\\frac{4}{5}. \\]\n\n**Case 2: \\( \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = -4 \\)**\n\nMultiply both sides by \\( 3x-4 \\):\n\n\\[ 4x - 16 = -4(3x - 4) \\]\n\\[ 4x - 16 = -12x + 16 \\]\n\\[ 4x + 12x = 16 + 16 \\]\n\\[ 16x = 32 \\]\n\\[ x = 2. \\]\n\nThe possible values of \\( x \\) are \\( -\\frac{4}{5} \\) and \\( 2 \\). The greatest possible value of \\( x \\) is \\( 2 \\).\n\nThus, the greatest possible value of \\( x \\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
